// World events: one-off things that happen to the whole town on a day and change it for good
// (crates/sim/src/events.rs). Weather is not here: it follows from the clock (weather.ron).
//
// Each event:
//   id       unique; what MCP (`events`, `trigger_event`, `schedule_event`) calls it
//   name     a short name for lists
//   message  what every survivor is told when it happens ("" for nothing)
//   days     (from, to): game days after the world began; it happens at a time in between, picked
//            from the world's loot seed, so the same world always has the same day and a new game
//            another
//   chance   the chance it happens at all in a world (default 1: always)
//   effect   Notice (the message only), WaterOff, WaterOn, PowerOff, PowerOn
//   warn     Some((hours, "words")): a warning that many game hours before
//
// WaterOn and PowerOn are for putting things back by hand: `trigger_event` (MCP, or a hosted
// server's admin endpoint). Their days are far off and their chance 0, so they never happen by
// themselves. No file: no events.
(
    events: [
        (id: "water_off", name: "The water goes off", days: (3.0, 7.0), effect: WaterOff,
            message: "The taps cough and run dry. The town's water is off.",
            warn: Some((6.0, "The water pressure is dropping. Fill what you can."))),
        (id: "power_off", name: "The power goes off", days: (2.0, 5.0), effect: PowerOff,
            message: "The lights die all over town. The power is off.",
            warn: Some((3.0, "The lights flicker and dim. The grid won't hold much longer."))),
        (id: "water_on", name: "The water comes back", days: (3650.0, 3650.0), chance: 0.0, effect: WaterOn,
            message: "Water spits from the taps again."),
        (id: "power_on", name: "The power comes back", days: (3650.0, 3650.0), chance: 0.0, effect: PowerOn,
            message: "The lights come back on."),
    ],
)
